  "worked_solution": "Our task is to find $B$ such that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{43{x}^{2}+4x+2}{(6{x}^{2}+1)(x-1)}=\\frac{x+B}{6{x}^{2}+1}+\\frac{7}{x-1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides by $(6{x}^{2}+1)(x-1)$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}43{x}^{2}+4x+2 & =(x+B)(x-1)+7(6{x}^{2}+1).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor $x=0$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}43(0)^{2}+4(0)+2 & =(0+B)(0-1)+7(6(0)^{2}+1) \\\\ 2 & =-B+7 \\\\ B & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\n\\frac{43{x}^{2}+4x+2}{(6{x}^{2}+1)(x-1)}=\\frac{x+5}{6{x}^{2}+1}+\\frac{7}{x-1}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
